The rivers dataset, 2026 edition, is derived from HydroRIVERS line layers, which represent a subset of the HydroSHEDS database based on the 15 arc-second Digital Elevation Model (DEM) from NASA's Shuttle Radar Topography Mission (SRTM). 

The HydroRIVERS source data, developed on behalf of World Wildlife Fund US (WWF), Washington, DC, USA, in collaboration with McGill University, Montreal, Canada, represents a vectorized line network of all global rivers that have a catchment area of at least 10 km² or an average river flow of at least 0.1 m³/sec, or both. More information at https://www.hydrosheds.org/products/hydrorivers

The present dataset additionally incorporates a perennial/intermittent flow-regime classification (from 1 to 6) derived from HydroATLAS indicators and applied to the HydroRIVERS network. The classification distinguishes perennial and intermittent rivers reaches using climatic (Upstream aridity index: ari_ix_uav), hydrological (Minimum monthly discharge: dis_m3_pmn), and topological (Stream flow order: ORD_FLOW) indicators and has been further refined through network-topology smoothing to improve spatial consistency. 

Other key attributes include: 

- HYRIV_ID: unique identifier for each river reach; 

- NEXT_DOWN: identifier of the next downstream reach, supporting network connectivity analyses; 

- ORD_FLOW: river flow order based on discharge classes; 

- LENGTH_KM: reach length (km); 

- DIST_UP_KM and DIST_DN_KM: distance to source and outlet, respectively; 

- UPLAND_SKM: total upstream drainage area (km²); 

- CATCH_SKM: local catchment area (km²); 

- DIS_AV_CMS: long-term average discharge (m³/s).

